+## Class-rank audit — recommendation only, October 13
+
+`C:/Users/verre/.codex/worktrees/aa-tbs-policy/EQ_Local_Dev/docs/audits/aa-class-ranks-20261013/README.md`
+replaces the blanket three-rank recommendation with 26 explicitly reviewed lines:
+Slay Undead has nine contiguous in-era ranks (60 points plus Combat Fury3),
+Master Wu5, and deeper pet/caster/healer/class progression. Target catalog394
+families/1051 ranks preserves all941 currently allowed identities and level1
+access. This is not deployed or encounter-validated; live policy remains above.
+
+Triple Backstab's native roll is behind DoubleBackstabLevelRequirement55,
+confirmed on OVH against global MaxLevel50. Rank9 is conditional on a scoped
+native activation repair and level1/50 regression, not just a policy edit.
+Slay also amplifies physical skill hits such as kicks; test PAL/MNK coupling.
+Poison Mastery's application-time effect is a retained native no-op. Pet crit,
+pet flurry, distinct double-attack and spell-critical lines stack across held
+classes; do not infer balance from one class or a rank count. Free knight-touch
+and Hunter's Attack Power ranks need explicit treatment. Three newly satisfiable
+burn/heal dependencies remain blocked in the target scenario; four passive
+families are intentionally restored. See dependency-unlocks.csv and review.md.
+
+THJ's indexed Monk documentation confirms rank5 and later Master Wu progression;
+its exact Slay cap was not verified. Do not substitute THJ combat rules, level
+autogrants or another emulator's AA database for Nightcap data. The generator
+checks current pool, prerequisite closure, identity preservation and level1;
+source-evidence.json pins six retained files to the live build manifest. The
+fresh AA/rule checks do not refresh the whole spell snapshot or prove fun.
+Implementation would require the Rogue source fix, generated policy/header,
+matching zone build/guarded runtime rollout and signed patch notes; no client
+binary change anticipated. Preserve saved purchases and test restored usability.
